# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill-2 window (the device-side hand-off of the final step's GDN state; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-pf2-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same
# in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix steps (AP1, R1, R2) do not forward the selection into their container and serve the base checkpoint: the hand-off moves
# the GDN state of a finished prefill, whose shape and bytes the checkpoint does not change.
# T1 (TIMED, the CONTROL of the first smoke pair): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf2-s4-ctl, the approved ship-4 profile with the gate marker for its waiver
# id and QWEN_FAST_PREFILL_HANDOFF=0: the host path of the final step, byte for byte production's, which also prints the "[PF2] handoff mode=host" timing line, on Swift.
# Tests: warmup; coding (one user); parked_turns (eight seats, forty closed-loop turns of 4k to 24k tokens: forty final steps, each a hand-off beside seven decoding seats);
# prefill_ladder_solo (one request at a time at about 4k, 32k, 128k and 254k tokens: four final steps); concurrent8_steady (eight users: eight final steps, then the octo
# rounds, which the lever never touches). Every boot a fresh reset. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no
# other job beside it. CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...:
# found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step;
# the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration
# (estimate): 45 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf2-s4-ctl
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,parked_turns,prefill_ladder_solo,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=80
